pokeplatinum-speed.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the port's per-part speed options
(docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"), hooked where Platinum's C decides each part's pace; each hook asks
port/game/speed_gen4.c, which reads the same settings Black's and Black 2's stand-ins read. At every default setting each hook
is exactly the game's own code path, so the route chain's frames are unchanged.
Text speed: text.c SysTask_RunTextPrinter (the task every timed text printer runs once a frame: the field's and the battle's
messages, menus, every Options-speed caller and the fixed-speed ones) renders through PortTextSpeed_Render, which at Faster /
Fastest / Instant (4 / 8 / 1024 characters, PortSpeed4_TextChars) draws that many plain characters in the frame, clearing the
character wait before each; a control code, callback, key wait, scroll, pause or the end stops the frame as the game's one
render did. Instant printers (TEXT_SPEED_INSTANT) never reach the task and are unchanged. The DS build never sees the patch.
diff --git a/src/text.c b/src/text.c
index 0d8040c09..ca7a66935 100644
--- a/src/text.c
+++ b/src/text.c
@@ -226,4 +226,35 @@ u8 Text_AddPrinter(const TextPrinterTemplate *template, u32 renderDelay, TextPri
 }
 
+// bw-port: Text speed (the port's setting; docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"). At Faster, Fastest
+// or Instant a printer's frame draws up to that many characters with no wait between them (port/game/speed_gen4.c says how
+// many); at the game's own speed (0, the default) it is the one render a frame it always was. Only plain characters repeat:
+// a control code, a callback, a wait for a key, a scroll, a pause or the end stop the frame exactly as before.
+int PortSpeed4_TextChars(void);
+
+static enum RenderResult PortTextSpeed_Render(TextPrinter *printer)
+{
+    int n = PortSpeed4_TextChars();
+    int printed = 0;
+    enum RenderResult result;
+
+    if (n == 0) {
+        return TextPrinter_Render(printer);
+    }
+    for (;;) {
+        if (printer->state == 0) {   // handling characters: no wait before the next one
+            printer->delayCounter = 0;
+        }
+        result = TextPrinter_Render(printer);
+        if (result != RENDER_PRINT || --n <= 0 || printer->state != 0 || printer->callbackParam != 0) {
+            break;
+        }
+        printed = 1;
+    }
+    if (printed && result != RENDER_PRINT) {   // this frame's earlier characters reach the screen (RENDER_PRINT's copy)
+        Window_CopyToVRAM(printer->template.window);
+    }
+    return result;
+}
+
 static void SysTask_RunTextPrinter(SysTask *task, void *data)
 {
@@ -238,5 +269,5 @@ static void SysTask_RunTextPrinter(SysTask *task, void *data)
         Text_GenerateFontHalfRowLookupTable(printer->template.fgColor, printer->template.bgColor, printer->template.shadowColor);
 
-        switch (TextPrinter_Render(printer)) {
